faint:
But scarcely had we reached the distant place,
When o’er the hills we heard a faint bell ringing;
A boy came running up with frightened face;

fairy:
And she never will be all mine;
She learned her hands in a fairy-tale,
And her mouth on a valentine.

fairies:
For some, godfather and goddame
The opulent fairies be;
Dame Poverty gave me my name,

failing:
And bring the uneven world back to its round;
Or, failing so much, fill up, bridge at least
To smoother issues, some abysmal cracks

fainting:
Not a soul to share her fate;
She was weary, he was fainting,
And life seemed so desolate.

faithless:
Forsooth, because the month was only May;
Be faithless of the kind of proffered love,
And captious, lest it miss my dignity,

And want consorts with crime;
Or men grown faithless sadly say
That evil is the time.

Oh, think not I am faithful to a vow!
Faithless am I save to love's self alone.
Were you not lovely I would leave you now;

faints:
In the Heavenly day:
Yet she flags and almost faints;
Can such be meant for me?

fairhaired:
Had dared to raise its head;
Not a fairhaired dandelion
Peeped timid from its bed;

fait:
Comme l'amour, comme la mort;
Et j'ai fait les plus belles de belle argile
Sèche et fragile.

faileth:
That sings on summer trees;
When his song faileth
And the ship saileth
